# RouteLeak — launch configuration
# Copy to `.env` for local development. Never commit real values or secrets.
#
# This Lovable app is the public/product UI. The preserved RouteLeak backend
# remains authoritative and today exposes:
#   POST/GET /api/uploads    field activity, invoice and payment exports
#   GET/POST /api/audits     reconciliation audits and their findings
#   GET/POST /api/pilots     pilot analysis requests and scoping
#   GET/POST /api/operator   operator workflow and job/failure operations
# It authenticates through its own secure workspace session, so this app does
# not hold credentials of any kind.
#
# Exactly one launch mode applies:
#
# 1) demo (default)
#    Leave every variable below empty. Synthetic, clearly labeled sample data
#    only. No network calls to any backend.
#
# 2) secure-link
#    Set VITE_SECURE_WORKSPACE_URL to the origin of the secure RouteLeak
#    workspace. Every real-analysis, sign-in and start CTA hands off to that
#    URL; no data is read from this app. Demo data is disabled.
VITE_SECURE_WORKSPACE_URL=

# 3) api  (future typed gateway — NOT the current backend contract)
#    Requires BOTH variables. A base URL on its own fails closed with a
#    configuration error; it never makes the app "Live". Only set these once a
#    same-origin gateway is deployed that:
#      - is served from this app's origin (or a CORS-approved origin) and
#        authenticates with the conventional session cookie
#        (credentials: "include", no API keys in the browser), and
#      - implements the typed v1 contract in src/lib/product-api/types.ts
#        (/v1/session, /v1/summary, /v1/runs, /v1/exceptions, ...), mapping the
#        preserved /api/uploads, /api/audits, /api/pilots and /api/operator
#        routes behind it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_API_CONTRACT_VERSION=
